Z||000000||mrfixit58||10-09-2000||06:50 PM||||Check out the pics from the Old Town Car show. <BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=446733&a=9289881" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=446733&a=9289881</A> <P>My club, Sun Coast Fieros had six cars in competition and nine cars in attendance. Central Florida and Space Coast each had two. Here's a sample (My little car of course   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ):<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BlueBellTrophy_1.jpg"> <P>Roy   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by mrfixit58 (edited 10-09-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-09-2000||07:51 PM||||Who owns the Zimmer??||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||10-10-2000||07:17 AM||||Lar,<P>One of the guys in my club owns the Zimmer. I got to talk to him a little at the show. He said he bought it pretty much in the shape you see it now except for recovering the seat covers and the center console and detail work. I know it looks odd to most but up close and personal, it's really pretty cool. I was parked right behind him and, believe me, it gets LOTS of attention. I bet I heard "nice car" or "cool" at least 50 times.<P>He told me it's for sale.... only $24,000.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000003||Old Lar||10-10-2000||07:42 AM||||The Zimmers are quite rare and when new they were $50,000 +.  A professionally manufactured rebody car. It is one of those cars you either love or hate.  It does show the versatility of the Fiero space age frame and different cars styles that could be derived from it. (like the Jalapino from Pisa).  I wish I had a few extra $Ks around and a place to store it.||||reg||10
Z||000004||Songman||10-10-2000||10:10 AM||||That's cool! I have seen the big Zimmers before but I never knew they did one on a Fiero!||||reg||14
